From 450fef016d5d9c848a92b041b29f844a008f1e78 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tnikkel <tnikkel@mozilla.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 00:50:56 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Only build a ready rectangle after checking that it is
 non-empty

`ready_image_area` builds the `Rect` eagerly rather than lazily, so the size
subtractions run on the rectangles the guard rejects, overflowing where checks
are on.

The guard is false for a group column narrower than the border, which has no
interior of its own: at 513 wide with 256 pixel groups and a 3 pixel border the
last column is 1 pixel, x0 is 515 and x1 clamps to 513. It needs the group
marked ready before its left neighbour, which happens under parallel decoding
and in a chunked single threaded decode.

narrow_edge_group.jxl is 513x321 lossy RGBA. The width gives the narrow last
column; alpha and lossy are both needed to reproduce.

Local backport scope: production changes only. Upstream regression tests,
fixtures, and test-only harness changes are intentionally omitted. The
original commit message above describes the full upstream change.

diff --git a/jxl/src/render/low_memory_pipeline/group_scheduler.rs b/jxl/src/render/low_memory_pipeline/group_scheduler.rs
--- a/jxl/src/render/low_memory_pipeline/group_scheduler.rs
+++ b/jxl/src/render/low_memory_pipeline/group_scheduler.rs
@@ -113,7 +113,7 @@ fn ready_image_area(
     }
     .min(input_size.0);
 
-    (x1 >= x0 && y1 >= y0).then_some(Rect {
+    (x1 >= x0 && y1 >= y0).then(|| Rect {
         origin: (x0, y0),
         size: (x1 - x0, y1 - y0),
     })
